=0) is just y.\n\nDistance to side 2 (y = -\u221a3x + \u221a3 a). The formula for distance from (x,y) to line Ax + By + C = 0 is |Ax + By + C| / sqrt(A^2 + B^2). Let's rewrite side 2's equation: \u221a3x + y - \u221a3 a = 0. So A = \u221a3, B = 1, C = -\u221a3 a. Distance is |\u221a3 x + y - \u221a3 a| / sqrt( (\u221a3)^2 + 1^2 ) = |\u221a3 x + y - \u221a3 a| / 2.\n\nSimilarly, distance to side 3 (y = \u221a3 x) can be written as \u221a3 x - y = 0. So distance is |\u221a3 x - y| / sqrt( (\u221a3)^2 + (-1)^2 ) = |\u221a3 x - y| / 2.\n\nSo the three distances are:\n\nd1 = y,\n\nd2 = |\u221a3 x + y - \u221a3 a| / 2,\n\nd3 = |\u221a3 x - y| / 2.\n\nBut since the point is inside the triangle, all these distances should be positive, and the expressions inside the absolute values should have consistent signs. Let's consider the position of the point (x,y). Inside the triangle, so below the two other sides.\n\nFor side 2: y = -\u221a3x + \u221a3 a. The point is below this line, so y <= -\u221a3x + \u221a3 a. Therefore, \u221a3 x + y - \u221a3 a <= 0. Hence, |\u221a3 x + y - \u221a3 a| = -(\u221a3 x + y - \u221a3 a) = \u221a3 a - \u221a3 x - y. So d2 = (\u221a3 a - \u221a3 x - y)/2.\n\nFor side 3: y = \u221a3 x. The point is below this line as well, so y <= \u221a3 x. Therefore, \u221a3 x - y >= 0, so |\u221a3 x - y| = \u221a3 x - y. Hence, d3 = (\u221a3 x - y)/2.\n\nTherefore, the three distances are:\n\nd1 = y,\n\nd2 = (\u221a3 a - \u221a3 x - y)/2,\n\nd3 = (\u221a3 x - y)/2.\n\nNow, according to the problem, these distances are 3, 4, 5 in some order. But the problem doesn't specify which distance corresponds to which side, so we have to consider all permutations. However, since the triangle is equilateral and symmetric, the result should be the same regardless of the order. But maybe we need to set up equations accordingly.\n\nBut maybe there's a smarter way. Let's sum up the three distances:\n\nd1 + d2 + d3 = y + (\u221a3 a - \u221a3 x - y)/2 + (\u221a3 x - y)/2.\n\nLet'