)\\).\n   - Vector \\(CM\\) is \\(\\left(\\frac{\\cos(\\theta + 24^\\circ) - \\cos\\theta}{2}, \\frac{\\sin\\theta + \\sin(\\theta + 24^\\circ)}{2}\\right)\\).\n\n5. **Trigonometric Identities**:\n   - Using trigonometric identities, we simplify the components of vector \\(CM\\):\n     - \\(\\cos(\\theta + 24^\\circ) - \\cos\\theta = -2 \\sin(\\theta + 12^\\circ) \\sin 12^\\circ\\)\n     - \\(\\sin\\theta + \\sin(\\theta + 24^\\circ) = 2 \\sin(\\theta + 12^\\circ) \\cos 12^\\circ\\)\n\n6. **Magnitudes and Dot Product**:\n   - Magnitude of \\(CA\\) is \\(\\sin\\theta\\).\n   - Magnitude of \\(CM\\) is \\(\\sin(\\theta + 12^\\circ)\\).\n   - Dot product \\(CA \\cdot CM\\) simplifies to \\(\\sin\\theta \\sin(\\theta + 12^\\circ) \\cos 12^\\circ\\).\n\n7. **Angle Calculation**:\n   - Using the dot product formula, \\(\\cos \\phi = \\frac{CA \\cdot CM}{|CA| |CM|}\\) simplifies to \\(\\cos 12^\\circ\\), leading to \\(\\phi = 12^\\circ\\).\n\n8. **Conclusion**:\n   - Regardless of the position of \\(AB\\) on the semicircle, the angle \\(\\angle ACM\\) is always \\(12^\\circ\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12^\\circ}\n\\]", "ground_truth_solution": "\nWe are given that the skateboard ramp is in the shape of a semicircle with diameter \\(PQ\\), and \\(AB\\) is the segment that Tony Hawk is skating on. \\(M\\) is the midpoint of \\(AB\\), and \\(C\\) is the foot of the perpendicular from \\(A\\) to \\(PQ\\). We need to find the possible values of the angle \\(\\angle ACM\\), given that the arc \\(AB\\) is \\(24^\\circ\\).\n\n1. **Extend \\(AC\\) to intersect the semicircle at point \\(D\\)**. According to the problem statement's diagram, point \\(D\\) lies on the semicircle such that \\(AD\\) is perpendicular to \\(PQ\\).\n\n2. **Analyze the properties of the semicircle and \\(AD\\)**:\n   - \\(AD\\) is perpendicular to the diameter \\(PQ\\).\n   - Therefore, \\(AD\\) bisects \\(PQ\\) at point \\(C\\) because in a semicircle, a perpendicular from any point on the circle to the diameter b